{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And it shall come to pass, etc.</b> If concerning the Messiah, that the entire world is under his authority, and according to the opinion of R. Moses the Hakohen mentioned in connection with the sign of the sun, for thus it is written to seek the portent (2 Chronicles 32:31):" "<b>And his resting place shall be glory.</b> In glory. Likewise what is found: the House of YHWH (2 Kings 18:16):"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The phrase 'the sign of the sun' likely refers to the sun's retreat in Hezekiah's day; the parenthetical citation immediately following supports the reference.", 1 "The second example is textually compressed; Ibn Ezra apparently cites a phrase resembling 'the house of YHWH' from the 2 Kings passage to illustrate a similar construct use."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:27.960857699Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}